speechtext:
I lost sight of the fact
that to-day was Wednesday, and the House does not sit to-night. I must simply say this:	The motion must be disposed of;
otherwise, I do not know where we shall be on Friday.

What was formerly the
New Brunswick unit has been consolidated wdth the Halifax institution so that it is now only a sub-unit. The list of medical men employed in the St. John sub-unit comprises: Dr. Skinner, chief medical representative and consultant, who is engaged on full time at a salary of $4,000; the late Dr. McCarthy, medical superintendent of Lancaster hospital; Dr. Pratt, pension examiner; Dr. Kirkland, medical officer; Dr. Malcolm, medical officer;
Dr. Nase, medical officer; Dr. Bridges, medical officer; Dr. White, medical officer Of these 7 medical men three are on full time and four part time and the salaries paid them amount to $18,640. One officer on part time receives $600 per year, namely, Dr. Kirkland.
